# api.business.govt.nz subscription keys, used by the dev API middleware
# (vite-api-plugin.ts) to emulate api/proxy.ts locally. In production these
# are set as Vercel environment variables instead — this file only matters
# for `npm run dev`.
ORG_NZBN_KEY=
ORG_COMPANIES_KEY=
ORG_DISQUALIFIED_KEY=
ORG_INSOLVENCY_KEY=

# Property search (api/property.ts) — LINZ Title Register.
#
# LINZ_API_KEY is a LINZ Data Service key. The titles/owners/memorials layers it
# reads are RESTRICTED personal data under the LINZ Licence for Personal Data.
#
# AUTH — one variable per person, holding that person's PASSWORD.
# (Fictional example — never write a real password into a committed file;
# real values live only in Vercel env vars / a local untracked .env.)
#
#   PROPERTY_PW_JANE_DOE_FBU_COM=not-a-real-password
#
# The variable name is the address uppercased with every run of
# non-alphanumerics collapsed to an underscore, so jane.doe@fbu.com becomes
# PROPERTY_PW_JANE_DOE_FBU_COM. `npm run property:user -- <email>` prints the
# name if you would rather not work it out by hand. Sign in with the address.
#
# One variable per person is what makes a reset safe: add, reset or revoke
# touches exactly that person's variable, and because the session is signed with
# a secret derived from their credential, a reset signs out only them.
#
# The value is the password in plain text, so it can be changed from the Vercel
# dashboard with no tooling. The trade: anyone who can read the environment
# reads the passwords. Fine for purpose-made credentials used only here; not
# fine for a password reused anywhere else. A `scrypt.<salt>.<key>` value is
# still accepted and verified as a hash, if you ever want that for an account.
#
# There is NO shared password. PROPERTY_PASS was removed: a credential that
# works for everybody is what per-user accounts exist to end, and as a silent
# fallback it made a misconfigured deployment look like everyone had simply
# typed their password wrong.
#
# LINZ_API_KEY plus at least one credential must be set, or /api/property
# returns 503 and the feature is unreachable. That is deliberate: it fails closed.
LINZ_API_KEY=
# PROPERTY_PW_SOMEONE_FBU_COM=their-password-here
